title: "Release Process"
description: "How qql-go releases are cut — version bump, validation, tagging, and binary publishing."
sidebar:
  order: 3
---

## Version Locations

Versions must be kept in sync:

| File | Format |
|---|---|
| `VERSION` | `X.Y.Z` |
| `internal/cli/commands/executor.go` | `var Version = "X.Y.Z"` |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | `## [X.Y.Z]` heading |
| `docs/releases/X.Y.Z.md` | Full release notes |

## Validation

Before tagging, run the release validator:

{% terminal title="Release Validation" %}
go run docs/dev_tasks.go release-validate --version X.Y.Z
{% /terminal %}

This checks:
1. `[1/4] Version sync` — VERSION file, commands.go, CHANGELOG all match
2. `[2/4] Quality checks` — `gofmt`, `go vet`, `go test ./...`, `go build`
3. `[3/4] Building binary` — confirms a clean binary builds
4. `[4/4] Binary version` — binary reports the correct version

All four checks must pass before tagging.

## Release Steps

{% terminal title="Release Process" %}
# 1. Update versions in all four locations
# 2. Write release notes in docs/releases/X.Y.Z.md
# 3. Update CHANGELOG.md
# 4. Validate
go run docs/dev_tasks.go release-validate --version X.Y.Z

# 5. Tag and push
git tag -a vX.Y.Z -m "Release X.Y.Z"
git push origin vX.Y.Z
{% /terminal %}

## CI/CD

GitHub Actions automatically:
- Runs `go test ./...` on every push
- Builds binaries for `linux/amd64`, `linux/arm64`, `windows/amd64`, `darwin/arm64` on tag push
- Publishes binaries to GitHub Releases
- Generates `qql-go_X.Y.Z_checksums.txt`

## Binary Distribution

Release artifacts:

| Binary | Platform |
|---|---|
| `qql-go` | Linux amd64 |
| `qql-go` | Linux arm64 |
| `qql-go.exe` | Windows amd64 |
| `qql-go` | macOS arm64 |
| `qql-go_X.Y.Z_checksums.txt` | All platforms |

Install script (`install.sh`) and PowerShell script (`install.ps1`) auto-detect platform and download the correct binary.
